From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msi, msiexec: an install has an administrator's privileges only when it has them; one for all users without them stops with 1925, as Windows Installer does

Wine's msi said "in a wine environment the user is always admin and privileged": Privileged,
MsiRunningElevated, AdminUser and MsiTrueAdminUser were always 1. In a shared prefix a standard user
or an unelevated administrator then ran an all-users package as themselves, and it failed half way
on Program Files and HKLM (1603), or half installed. Windows Installer stops such an install before
it changes anything: error 1925 ("You do not have sufficient privileges to complete this
installation for all users"), 1730 for a removal.

- Privileged / MsiRunningElevated: the process is elevated, or holds a linked administrator's token
  it can use (Wine's own model in a prefix of one's own, where msi's custom action server uses it).
  AdminUser / MsiTrueAdminUser: that, or an administrator's session (SG_USER_ADMIN).
- InstallInitialize: a first install or a removal of an all-users product without those privileges
  stops with 1925 / 1730. A repair or change of an installed product goes on as before (Windows'
  Installer service does those with the privileges the product was installed with).
- ALLUSERS=2 with MSIINSTALLPERUSER=1 installs per user, as Windows Installer 5 resolves it (Wine
  made every ALLUSERS=2 an all-users install).
- msiexec never relaunches itself through the consent prompt in silent mode (/qn), for an all-users
  package either (0590 did): Windows Installer cannot ask there. SG Store elevates the MSIs it
  installs itself, so its silent installs keep working.

David 2026-11-23: as Windows does it. Gate test-msipriv (test/msipriv-gate.sh); mutants
SG_MUTANT_MSI_ALWAYS_PRIVILEGED, SG_MUTANT_MSI_NO_1925, SG_MUTANT_MSIEXEC_QN_RELAUNCH.
test-msiallusers now installs with basic UI.
---
--- a/dlls/msi/action.c
+++ b/dlls/msi/action.c
@@ -3082,9 +3082,36 @@
     return ERROR_SUCCESS;
 }
 
+/* Stained Glass OS 9002: installing or removing a product for all users needs an administrator's
+ * privileges, as Windows Installer requires: without them it stops before changing anything, with
+ * error 1925 -- 1730 for a removal -- where Wine went on as the user and failed half way on Program Files and HKLM. msiexec
+ * asks for consent first (0590) except in silent mode, where Windows Installer cannot ask either. */
 static UINT ACTION_InstallInitialize(MSIPACKAGE *package)
 {
+    MSIRECORD *record;
+    WCHAR *remove;
+    BOOL removing;
+
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_MSI_NO_1925
+    if (package->Context != MSIINSTALLCONTEXT_MACHINE || msi_sg_privileged()) return ERROR_SUCCESS;
+    remove = msi_dup_property( package->db, L"REMOVE" );
+    removing = remove && !wcsicmp( remove, L"ALL" );
+    free( remove );
+    /* a repair or a change of an installed product (its own self-repair, on Windows done by the
+     * Installer service with the privileges it was installed with) goes on as before */
+    if (!removing && MsiQueryProductStateW( package->ProductCode ) == INSTALLSTATE_DEFAULT) return ERROR_SUCCESS;
+    WARN( "an install for all users without an administrator's privileges: error %u\n",
+          removing ? MSIERR_ADMIN_TO_REMOVE : MSIERR_NOT_PRIVILEGED );
+    if ((record = MSI_CreateRecord( 1 )))
+    {
+        MSI_RecordSetInteger( record, 1, removing ? MSIERR_ADMIN_TO_REMOVE : MSIERR_NOT_PRIVILEGED );
+        MSI_ProcessMessage( package, INSTALLMESSAGE_ERROR, record );
+        msiobj_release( &record->hdr );
+    }
+    return ERROR_INSTALL_FAILURE;
+#else
     return ERROR_SUCCESS;
+#endif
 }
 
 
